---
import HelpLayout from '../../layouts/HelpLayout.astro';
import HelpMedia from '../../components/HelpMedia.astro';
import { DESKTOP_INSTALL_URL, WEB_INSTALL_URL } from '../../consts';
---

<HelpLayout title="Use Folio AI in PowerPoint" active="powerpoint" description="Install the Folio AI add-in in PowerPoint, sign in, and generate your first presentation.">
  <p>
    Folio AI runs as an add-in inside PowerPoint, so it works right next to your slides with nothing
    to download to your computer. It's supported on <strong>PowerPoint for Microsoft 365</strong>,
    <strong>PowerPoint 2021 and 2019</strong>, and <strong>PowerPoint on the web</strong>, on both
    Windows and Mac. Follow the steps below to get set up.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Get the Folio AI add-in</h2>
  <p>There are two ways to install Folio in PowerPoint:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>From PowerPoint (recommended).</strong> Open PowerPoint, go to the
      <strong>Home</strong> or <strong>Insert</strong> tab, select <strong>Add-ins</strong> (or
      <strong>Get Add-ins</strong>), search for <strong>Folio AI</strong>, and choose
      <strong>Add</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>From the Microsoft AppSource store.</strong> You can also install Folio directly from
      Microsoft's store, then return to PowerPoint. <a href={WEB_INSTALL_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the Folio AI listing on AppSource →</a>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Already have PowerPoint installed? You can <a href={DESKTOP_INSTALL_URL}>open Folio in the
    desktop app</a> directly.
  </p>
  <HelpMedia src="/help/powerpoint-1.png" caption="Searching for Folio AI under Home → Add-ins in PowerPoint." />

  <h2>2. Launch Folio AI</h2>
  <p>
    After installing, the Folio AI button appears in your PowerPoint ribbon (usually on the
    <strong>Home</strong> tab). Select it to open the Folio side panel next to your slides. If you
    don't see it right away, restart PowerPoint and check again.
  </p>
  <HelpMedia src="/help/powerpoint-2.png" caption="The Folio AI button in the PowerPoint ribbon." />

  <h2>3. Sign in to your Folio account</h2>
  <p>
    In the side panel, sign in to your Folio account. Your Folio account is separate from your
    Microsoft account, so you can sign in with whichever method you prefer. If this is your first
    time, you'll create an account in a few seconds.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Start with your free credits</h2>
  <p>
    Every new account includes <strong>500 free credits</strong> with <strong>no credit card
    required</strong>, so you can try Folio right away. When you need more, you can choose a plan at
    any time — see <a href="/help/plans-and-billing/">Plans and Billing</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Generate your first presentation</h2>
  <p>
    With the panel open, describe the deck you want — or open an existing presentation and ask Folio
    to edit it. Folio uses your current template's fonts, colors, and layouts so the result stays on
    brand. You can keep refining with follow-up prompts, and make manual edits in PowerPoint at any
    point since every shape stays fully editable.
  </p>
  <HelpMedia src="/help/powerpoint-3.png" caption="Entering a prompt in the Folio panel to generate a deck." />

  <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
  <p>
    Add-in not appearing, sign-in problems, or restrictions on a work account? See the
    <a href="/help/troubleshooting/">Troubleshooting</a> guide, or
    <a href="/help/get-support/">get in touch with our team</a>.
  </p>
</HelpLayout>
